cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CircaGrowth, please cite it as below."
title: "CircaGrowth: an ODE model of circadian rhythm, glucose, insulin and growth-hormone (STH) dynamics"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Abdullayev
    given-names: Omar
    affiliation: "School No. 39 named after M. C. Pashayev, Ganja, Azerbaijan"
repository-code: "https://github.com/omaraabdul10-coder/circagrowth"
url: "https://omaraabdul10-coder.github.io/circagrowth/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - computational physiology
  - circadian rhythm
  - growth hormone
  - insulin
  - meal timing
  - ordinary differential equations
abstract: >-
  CircaGrowth couples a Bergman-type glucose-insulin model with a circadian
  growth-hormone (STH) secretion term to study how meal timing interacts with
  nocturnal STH secretion. In the current model, a 23:00 dinner lowers the
  simulated STH peak by about 1%, and a meal about 45 minutes before the peak
  lowers it by about 14%. The model is a hypothesis-generation tool, not
  validated against human data and not medical advice.
